From d4243989b029d924ec28dc5b46a0e24b4c749e29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: overdoingism <overdoingism@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:10:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] speculative: DFlash2 adaptive verify width (opt-in), aligned
 across the sequences drafted together

With LLAMA_DFLASH_ADAPTIVE=1, a DFlash2 sequence drafts w tokens and sends them to verification; w follows per-position
acceptance estimates towards the width with the most accepted tokens per unit of step time.  Unset or 0, nothing
changes.

The step time is measured, not modelled: for each width a request has run at, the time from the start of one draft of
the sequence to the start of its next (its draft, the verification and whatever else the step held), averaged over the
width's last 8 steps; a step more than 4x the width's average is left out as holding other work.  A width with fewer
than 4 such steps is costed by a model (0.09 of the step's fixed part per verified row, 0.15 with an active expert-cache
arena, no cheaper below 4 rows), scaled to the nearest measured width.  So the model only proposes a move and the
measurement at the new width decides whether it stays: a move whose saving falls short is undone at the next decision.

It moves one width at a time and only on what it has seen.  Down: for an estimated gain above 3 %, not before 24 drafts
of a request and then 8 at the new width, and only if the narrower width still wins with the positions observed in
fewer than 2 drafts taken as accepted (no move on an extrapolated tail).  Up: for a gain above 1 %, once the position
past w is observed (every 4th draft carries one token past w).  A sequence keeps w into a request whose prompt continues
its last one (the last prompt's 32 tokens ending 16 before its end appear at the same place: the next turn of a
conversation, or the same prompt again); any other request starts from n_max (or --spec-draft-n-start).

The estimates come from the sequence's history: at its next draft, the last draft is compared with the tokens the target
produced after it (a draft token equal to the target's token at its position is one the verification accepts, under
greedy match and under rejection sampling alike).  Per position they are decayed counts (P(k accepted | k-1 accepted) =
hits / checks) with two pseudo-checks at the previous position's estimate.  Nothing hooks accept() / accept_partial().

On a hybrid or recurrent target (spec_align_enabled(), issue #234), the sequences drafted in one call send one width,
the widest among them, bounded by the lowest hard cap of the call and by the expert cache's verify band, as
align_draft_caps() does for draft-mtp-adaptive.  No cut of finished drafts.

LLAMA_DFLASH_ADAPTIVE=2 also logs the width changes; LLAMA_SPEC_ALIGN=0 drops the alignment;
LLAMA_DFLASH_ADAPTIVE_COST / _JUMP / _FLOOR override the model.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
